{"obsah":"<p>We've organised day camps and we train men, but women were somewhat missing from our portfolio. Together with Katarína Tóthová we prepared a camp exclusively for the fairer sex – though I'd probably start calling them something else. Although registration again opened only a few weeks in advance, 10 brave Amazons signed up who wanted to improve their riding technique, and even learn how to repair a bike.</p>\n\n<p>The whole morning was devoted to basic technique, riding over sleepers, body position on the bike, the pump track (i.e. rollers and berms) and the trail in our park. Then we moved to the popular Říčany restaurant Na Jurečku to refuel and rehydrate. And after lunch it was straight out into the terrain for descents, roots and even a hint of dropping. </p>\n\n<p>We have to take our hats off to everyone, because on the same terrain many men would at least hesitate or get off the bike. They simply went for it with heart and encouragement.&nbsp; After returning to the park there was a final workshop by Mára Tryner focused on bike repair and maintenance, and a look at the MALOJA 2021 collection. </p>\n\n<p>Thanks to everyone for taking part – we'll answer questions about the next date within a few days :)</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2020%2F08%2F20200816_104755-1.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"174878\" data-full-url=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2020%2F08%2F20200816_104755-1.webp?alt=media\" data-link=\"https://bikeskills.cz/?attachment_id=174878\" class=\"wp-image-174878\"/></figure></li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2020%2F